pragma language_version 0.23;

import CompactStandardLibrary;

// ===========================================================================
// datum v2 — realisable-value solvency attestation, with venue provenance
// and a chained attestation history
// ===========================================================================
//
// Proves: the depth-adjusted realisable value of a private lending book covers
// its private debt at a PUBLIC required collateral ratio, against PUBLIC venue
// reserves that are bound to a specific on-chain pool event. Publishes the
// verdict, the venue provenance and the history. Publishes no position.
//
// What changed since v1 (Wave 1):
//   1. Venues carry provenance. Each slot names an EVM chain, a constant-
//      product pool, the Sync log its reserves came from (block, tx, log
//      index), and a reference block. All of it is a public input and is
//      written to the ledger, so a verifier re-fetches that exact log.
//   2. Freshness is enforced by the Midnight ledger, not trusted. The circuit
//      asserts, through kernel block-time queries in the public transcript,
//      that the attestation lands within maxRefAge seconds after the
//      reference block's timestamp.
//   3. The swap fee is in the bound. v1 used Y*q/(X+q), which ignores the
//      pool fee and therefore let a prover claim slightly more than a real
//      sale returns. v2 uses the exact constant-product-with-fee output.
//   4. The same pool cannot be listed twice. Splitting one sale across two
//      copies of the same pool would undercount price impact, so active
//      slots must name distinct (chain, pool) pairs.
//   5. Only the registered attestor can attest, and every attestation is
//      chained to the previous one: its commitment includes the previous
//      head and the period number, and the circuit requires the attestor to
//      prove knowledge of the previous period's opening.
//   6. A slot may be quoted in a priced asset, not only a USD stablecoin.
//      Each slot carries a PUBLIC quoteRate (USD per whole quote token), and
//      proceeds are valued at it. 1.0 for USDC; for WETH, Moonwell's oracle
//      price at refBlock, which the verifier re-reads from Base.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// SCALE CONVENTION
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Quantities are MICRO-UNITS (1e-6 of one whole token), normalised off-chain
// from raw token units with the token's decimals. The verifier repeats the
// normalisation from the raw Sync log, so the rule is fixed and conservative:
//   reserveX (collateral side) = ceil (raw * 1e6 / 10^decX)   -> rounds UP
//   reserveY (quote side)      = floor(raw * 1e6 / 10^decY)   -> rounds DOWN
// Rounding X up and Y down can only understate proceeds, never overstate.
// Normalised quantities are capped at 2^64 (~1.8e13 whole tokens).
//
// Proceeds p are in QUOTE micro-units. quoteRate is USD micro-units per WHOLE
// quote token (USDC: 1_000_000; WETH at $2,558.36: 2_558_358_868), so
//   p * quoteRate  is USD in units of 1e-12, the same scale as
//   debt * requiredRatio (USD micro-units times RATIO_SCALE).
// For a WETH-quoted slot this values the WETH leg AT THE MARK: the circuit
// prices the collateral's depth exactly and the WETH's at its oracle price.
// That assumption is stated, not hidden; the README measures WETH's own depth
// to back it.
//
// RATIO_SCALE = 1_000_000. requiredRatio is the ratio times RATIO_SCALE.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// OVERFLOW BUDGET
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Uint<n> is Uint<0..2^n> with an EXCLUSIVE upper bound. FEE_SCALE = 10000.
//
//   q, X, Y, p, debt                < 2^64
//   g = FEE_SCALE - feeBps           < 2^14
//   X * FEE_SCALE                    < 2^78
//   q * g                            < 2^78
//   X * FEE_SCALE + q * g            < 2^79
//   p * (X * FEE_SCALE + q * g)      < 2^143   per-slot LHS, widest term
//   Y * q * g                        < 2^142   per-slot RHS
//   p * quoteRate                    < 2^128
//   sum over 4 slots                 < 2^130
//   debt * requiredRatio             < 2^128
//
// Per-slot accumulators are Uint<160>: 17 bits over the widest term. The
// compiler's ceiling is Uint<248>.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT THE CIRCUIT CANNOT CHECK, AND WHO DOES
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// A Midnight circuit cannot read another chain. Three provenance facts are
// therefore checked by the verifier against a public RPC, using the values
// this contract binds and publishes:
//   (a) the log at (syncBlock, logIndex) in syncTx is a Sync from `pool`, and
//       its raw reserves normalise to exactly reserveX / reserveY;
//   (b) there is no later Sync from `pool` in (syncBlock:logIndex, refBlock],
//       so the reserves are the pool's state AT refBlock, not a deeper past
//       state picked on purpose;
//   (c) refTime is the timestamp of refBlock.
// The circuit enforces the parts that need no other chain: refTime is in the
// past and within maxRefAge of Midnight block time at inclusion; pools are
// distinct; fees are in range; padding contributes nothing.
// ===========================================================================

// One venue slot's PUBLIC state, provenance included.
//
// Field widths are part of the circuit budget. venueDigest is a SHA-256
// persistentHash over all four slots, so every byte added to a slot can add a
// whole compression block. Adding quoteRate as a Uint<64> took the circuit
// from 32,731 rows (k=15) to 35,209 (k=16), which doubles prover memory.
// Chain ids and block numbers are Uint<32> instead (4.29e9: about 272 years
// of 2-second Base blocks), which brings it back to 32,606 rows, k=15.
// Measured with `zkir mock-compile`.
//
// A slot is ACTIVE when chainId != 0. Padding slots use chainId 0 and must
// carry zero claimed proceeds.
export struct VenueSlot {
  chainId: Uint<32>;          // EIP-155 chain id (1 Ethereum, 8453 Base)
  pool: Bytes<20>;            // constant-product pool contract
  collateralIsToken0: Boolean;// which side of the pool the book sells
  decX: Uint<8>;              // decimals of the collateral token
  decY: Uint<8>;              // decimals of the quote token
  feeBps: Uint<16>;           // pool swap fee in basis points
  syncBlock: Uint<32>;        // block of the Sync log the reserves come from
  syncTx: Bytes<32>;          // transaction hash containing that log
  logIndex: Uint<32>;         // index of that log within its block
  refBlock: Uint<32>;         // reserves are claimed to be current AT this block
  refTime: Uint<64>;          // unix timestamp of refBlock
  reserveX: Uint<64>;         // collateral reserve, micro-units, rounded up
  reserveY: Uint<64>;         // quote reserve, micro-units, rounded down
  quoteRate: Uint<64>;        // USD micro-units per whole quote token
}

// The preimage of the book commitment. Including the previous head and the
// period makes the commitments a hash chain: a past attestation cannot be
// replaced, reordered or replayed at another period without breaking every
// later link.
struct BookPreimage {
  positions: Vector<4, Uint<64>>;
  debt: Uint<64>;
  prev: Bytes<32>;
  period: Uint<64>;
}

// The previous period's opening, supplied privately so the circuit can check
// the attestor still holds it. A lender who committed to an unopenable book
// cannot attest the next period.
export struct PrevOpening {
  positions: Vector<4, Uint<64>>;
  debt: Uint<64>;
  nonce: Bytes<32>;
}

// One period's public summary. Kept forever; the contract has no circuit that
// removes or rewrites an entry.
export struct AttestationRecord {
  commitment: Bytes<32>;
  prev: Bytes<32>;
  venuesHash: Bytes<32>;
  requiredRatio: Uint<64>;
  covered: Boolean;
  attestedAt: Uint<64>;
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// LEDGER — public state
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Number of attestations. Also the next period number.
export ledger attestationCount: Counter;

// hash(domain, attestorSecret). Only the holder of the secret can attest.
export ledger attestor: Bytes<32>;

// Maximum seconds between the reference block's timestamp and inclusion on
// Midnight. Fixed at deployment.
export ledger maxRefAge: Uint<32>;

// Chain head: the latest commitment, and the one before it (needed to
// recompute the previous commitment for the continuity check).
export ledger head: Bytes<32>;
export ledger prevHead: Bytes<32>;

// The period number the current head was committed at. Read back by the
// continuity check instead of computing `period - 1`: Compact evaluates BOTH
// sides of a conditional in the ZK circuit, so `period - 1` at period 0 wraps
// to r - 1 in the scalar field and reaches the hash as a malformed Uint<64>.
// The JS simulator skips the untaken branch and never sees it; the proof
// server rejects it ("Inputs did not match alignment"). Found on the local
// chain, 2026-10-08.
export ledger headPeriod: Uint<64>;

// Latest attestation, flattened for cheap reads.
export ledger bookCommitment: Bytes<32>;
export ledger venues: Vector<4, VenueSlot>;
export ledger venuesHash: Bytes<32>;
export ledger requiredRatio: Uint<64>;
export ledger covered: Boolean;
export ledger attestedAt: Uint<64>;

// Every period, keyed by period number.
export ledger history: Map<Uint<64>, AttestationRecord>;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WITNESSES — private state, never disclosed
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

witness positionSizes(): Vector<4, Uint<64>>;   // collateral sold per slot
witness claimedProceeds(): Vector<4, Uint<64>>; // claimed lower bound per slot
witness debtAmount(): Uint<64>;                 // USD micro-units
witness commitmentNonce(): Bytes<32>;           // fresh per period
witness attestorSecret(): Bytes<32>;            // the attestor's key
witness previousOpening(): PrevOpening;         // last period's opening

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// PURE HELPERS — exported so a verifier recomputes them with public data only
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

export pure circuit venueDigest(venueState: Vector<4, VenueSlot>): Bytes<32> {
  return persistentHash<Vector<4, VenueSlot>>(venueState);
}

export pure circuit attestorKey(sk: Bytes<32>): Bytes<32> {
  return persistentHash<Vector<2, Bytes<32>>>([pad(32, "datum:attestor:v2"), sk]);
}

pure circuit isActive(slot: VenueSlot): Boolean {
  return slot.chainId != 0;
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// CONSTRUCTOR
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

constructor(refAge: Uint<32>) {
  assert(refAge > 0, "datum: maxRefAge must be positive");
  // DISCLOSE: the attestor key is a hash of a secret, published so that
  // every later attestation can be checked against it. The secret is not.
  attestor = disclose(attestorKey(attestorSecret()));
  // DISCLOSE: a public deployment parameter.
  maxRefAge = disclose(refAge);
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE ATTESTATION
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
export circuit attest(
  venueState: Vector<4, VenueSlot>,
  ratio: Uint<64>,
  timestamp: Uint<64>
): [] {
  const q = positionSizes();
  const p = claimedProceeds();
  const debt = debtAmount();
  const nonce = commitmentNonce();

  // DISCLOSE: venueState is a public input — on-chain pool state plus the
  // coordinates of the log it came from — and it is written to the ledger
  // below. Disclosing it here, before any branch on it, is required because
  // whether a slot is active decides which kernel block-time queries run,
  // and those queries are visible in the public transcript.
  const vs = disclose(venueState);

  // --- who may attest ------------------------------------------------------
  assert(attestor == attestorKey(attestorSecret()), "datum: caller is not the registered attestor");

  assert(ratio != 0, "datum: requiredRatio must be positive");

  // --- the attestation time is Midnight's, not the caller's ----------------
  // attestedAt must be within 10 minutes of the block time at inclusion.
  const ts = disclose(timestamp);
  assert(ts > 600, "datum: timestamp out of range");
  assert(blockTimeGt((ts - 600) as Uint<64>), "datum: attestedAt is too far in the future");
  assert(blockTimeLt((ts + 600) as Uint<64>), "datum: attestedAt is too far in the past");

  const age = maxRefAge;

  for (const i of 0..4) {
    const slot = vs[i];

    // SOUNDNESS (carried from v1): X > 0 and Y > 0 on EVERY slot, padding
    // included. With q = 0 the per-slot bound reduces to p*X*FEE_SCALE <= 0,
    // which pins p to 0 only while X > 0.
    // Written as != 0: for an unsigned value it is the same test as > 0, and
    // an equality costs far fewer circuit rows than a range comparison.
    assert(slot.reserveX != 0, "datum: reserveX must be positive in every slot, padding included");
    assert(slot.reserveY != 0, "datum: reserveY must be positive in every slot, padding included");
    assert(slot.feeBps < 10000, "datum: feeBps must be below 10000");

    if (isActive(slot)) {
      // FRESHNESS, enforced by the ledger: the reference block's timestamp
      // is in the past, and inclusion happens within maxRefAge of it. These
      // are kernel queries in the public transcript, re-evaluated by the
      // node against the real block, so a prover cannot fake them.
      const rt = slot.refTime;
      assert(slot.refBlock >= slot.syncBlock, "datum: refBlock precedes the Sync it vouches for");
      // No positivity assert on quoteRate: a zero rate only understates
      // proceeds, so it can make a verdict falsely NOT COVERED, never falsely
      // COVERED. The verifier checks every rate against its source anyway.
      assert(blockTimeGt(rt), "datum: reference block is in the future");
      assert(blockTimeLt((rt + age) as Uint<64>), "datum: reference block is older than maxRefAge");

      // DISTINCT POOLS: listing one pool twice would let a sale be split
      // across two copies of the same depth and undercount its price impact.
      // Each unordered pair is checked once, from its lower index: a
      // duplicate needs both slots active, and the lower one is this branch.
      for (const j of 0..4) {
        if (j > i) {
          const other = vs[j];
          assert(
            !(isActive(other) && other.chainId == slot.chainId && other.pool == slot.pool),
            "datum: the same pool is listed in two slots"
          );
        }
      }
    } else {
      // PADDING contributes nothing. Belt and braces with the X > 0 rule.
      assert(p[i] == 0, "datum: a padding slot cannot claim proceeds");
    }

    // REALISABLE PROCEEDS WITH FEE. Selling q into (X, Y) with fee f returns
    //   Y * q * g / (X * FEE_SCALE + q * g),   g = FEE_SCALE - f.
    // The prover supplies p as a claimed lower bound; the circuit checks the
    // cross-multiplied form. Overclaiming fails here.
    const g = (10000 - slot.feeBps) as Uint<16>;
    const lhs: Uint<160> = p[i] * (slot.reserveX * 10000 + q[i] * g);
    const rhs: Uint<160> = slot.reserveY * q[i] * g;
    assert(lhs <= rhs, "datum: claimed proceeds exceed realisable proceeds for this slot");
  }

  // Proceeds valued in USD: quote micro-units times USD micro per quote token.
  const proceedsUsd =
    p[0] * vs[0].quoteRate + p[1] * vs[1].quoteRate +
    p[2] * vs[2].quoteRate + p[3] * vs[3].quoteRate;
  const isCovered = proceedsUsd >= debt * ratio;

  // --- the chain -----------------------------------------------------------
  const period = attestationCount.read();
  const currentHead = head;

  // CONTINUITY: from the second period on, the attestor proves knowledge of
  // the previous period's opening, privately. The opening never leaves the
  // circuit; only the fact that it matches the published head does.
  const prevOpen = previousOpening();
  if (period != 0) {
    const reopened = persistentCommit<BookPreimage>(
      BookPreimage {
        positions: prevOpen.positions,
        debt: prevOpen.debt,
        prev: prevHead,
        period: headPeriod
      },
      prevOpen.nonce
    );
    assert(reopened == currentHead, "datum: previous period's opening does not match the chain head");
  }

  // DISCLOSE: a hiding commitment over the private book, chained to the
  // previous head and the period number. What goes public is the commitment,
  // not the book.
  const commitment = disclose(persistentCommit<BookPreimage>(
    BookPreimage { positions: q, debt: debt, prev: currentHead, period: period },
    nonce
  ));

  const vh = venueDigest(vs);

  // DISCLOSE: the verdict — one bit derived from private p and debt, and the
  // single deliberate leak of the contract. The book, the debt and the
  // per-slot proceeds stay private.
  const verdict = disclose(isCovered);

  // DISCLOSE: the required ratio is public and fixed at attestation time.
  const r = disclose(ratio);

  prevHead = currentHead;
  head = commitment;
  headPeriod = period;
  bookCommitment = commitment;
  venues = vs;
  venuesHash = vh;
  requiredRatio = r;
  covered = verdict;
  attestedAt = ts;

  history.insert(
    period,
    AttestationRecord {
      commitment: commitment,
      prev: currentHead,
      venuesHash: vh,
      requiredRatio: r,
      covered: verdict,
      attestedAt: ts
    }
  );

  attestationCount.increment(1);
}
